Z||000000||Hank is Here||12-18-2000||02:32 PM||||this should be a simple question.  What is the best way to clean the tips?  Brillo?<P>thanks ||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||12-18-2000||02:44 PM||||steel wool seems to work nicely.  mine were filthy, i probably had never cleaned them.  i rubbed em with a little steel wool, and instantly they are nice and shiney.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||12-18-2000||04:08 PM||||mothers metal polish and a terry cloth rag... thats what I use.. mirror finish..  not sure about the stock ones.. mine is Stainless... I'm sure the stock ones are stainless too.. still chromish after 14+ years... on my GT there are stainless heat sheilds just above the exhaust tips.. you can polish them also!!! you can't really see them .. but just one more thing to be shiney and look new! <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Coconut||12-18-2000||04:17 PM||||Can heat discoloration be removed with steel wool or metal polish?  TIA  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000004||bHooper||12-18-2000||04:47 PM||||i haven't put a <B>lot</B> of elbow grease into mine, yet.  however most of the discoloration seems to be comping off, with the steel wool.<P>i also bought some kinda chrome cleaner... i will have to see what it is.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||12-18-2000||05:37 PM||||If you dont want to spend all day rubbing at it to get a lot of discoloration off, try sanding all the crap off with some emery cloth, and then using buffing compound to shine them up.  If the tips are still on your car, you'd probably have to use a small drill-mounted buffing wheel or a dremel.  They should come out great and shine up for a long time.  Then after that you can use the mother's chrome polish or something similar to maintain the finish.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Xtreme Fiero's||12-18-2000||10:31 PM||||If they are the tips on the my old 84 good luck geting those suckers back to chrome  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> they ar off of a 2M6 are they Chrome to begin with?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Hank is Here||12-18-2000||10:47 PM||||Sounds like lite abrasive is the best thing to use.  I just wanted to make sure that I would not be hurting the surface of the tip. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||12-19-2000||02:06 AM||||I used rubbing compund to remove stains and grime then Mothers polish for a mirror like finish.||||reg||1
